SPU: unwindable frame for the ig job kernel's job call (bisl lifted with --framed-bisl).

All 4 One 1.03 stalls at luminopolis: ig lane 0's host_depth (live lifted call brackets) rises ~386 per HUD reload
(351 -> 737 -> 1123 -> 1514 at the kernel idle pc 0x3F750, sp 0x3F450 each time) because a job (0x00D3C580) leaves
through the kernel's job-call return 0x3F8F4 from inside nested calls, and the drain continuations (patch 7039
interpreter fallback, resolver) keep running the kernel inside the dead job brackets. A bisl lifted with --framed-bisl
pushes {return_pc, depth, jmp_buf}; reaching that return pc from deeper longjmps back to the frame (dead host frames
dropped, depth/image/irq frame/pc restored), as the interrupt frame already does. Only kernels lifted with the flag
(tools/spu/lift_igjobs.py: the ig kernel, not the jobs) change; other titles' generated code is unchanged.
